`md:` prefixes only work on Tailwind-generated utility classes — a plain CSS class like `.test { background: red; }` isn't one, so `md:test` won't compile to anything (per `src/docs/responsive-design.mdx`, "Overview": *"This works for every utility class in the framework"*).

Fix: define it with `@utility` instead of a plain rule in `globals.css`:

```css
@utility test {
  background: red;
}
```

Then `<h3 className="md:test">` will work, since Tailwind can apply variants to custom utilities. Source: `src/docs/adding-custom-styles.mdx`, "Adding custom utilities → Simple utilities".

